that everybody get all the tokens you want.

72
00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.440
That's like the upward CFO conversation that you guys have magically not had.

73
00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:08.200
You will get an answer saying

74
00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.960
AI costs are getting harder to justify, people are more and more tokens.

75
00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.320
But me as a business leader, I'm

76
00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.720
not seeing how there's a link to actually moving faster on features.

77
00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.720
And that's the really, really big gap.

78
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.280
It's just throwing more LLM compute that's not fixed organization.

79
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.760
You actually want to be a native and give the people who can decide

80
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.280
the ability to execute

81
00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.960
Microsoft.

82
00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.600
And a similar phenomenon, they gave everybody cloud code.

83
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.360
And now they're taking it away.

84
00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.400
Because just giving cloud code to more

85
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.440
and more people in an organization is a wonderful way to burn money.

86
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.440
It is not the right way to speed up the work.

87
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.800
And now if we actually want to see like

88
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:52.720
what is all these token budget, where is this bending going to?

89
00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.080
Somebody is not a deep dive managing over 2400 companies and how they use AI.

90
00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.440
And you can see from any $100 that you spend on AI, only $18

91
